From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000046 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 13:45:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] banana-pi: program the BSS's basic rates into the kernel

OneWifi's 2.4 GHz BSSs advertise OFDM-only basic rates (6, 12 and 24
Mbit/s), but on the Banana Pi platform wifi_drv_set_ap never tells the
kernel: only a platform with PLATFORM_FLAGS_SET_BSS sends
NL80211_CMD_SET_BSS with NL80211_ATTR_BSS_BASIC_RATES, and only the
Intel platform sets it. The Banana Pi path, set_bss_param(), sends AP
isolation alone. mac80211's basic rate set stays empty, so it sends
beacons, broadcasts and probe responses at the band's lowest rate,
1 Mbit/s on 2.4 GHz: a 234-byte beacon takes 2,094 us of air instead
of 344 us. Measured in the lab (mac80211_hwsim, 9 October): all 7,501
beacons in 59 s from the 13 RDK BSSs on channel 6 went at 1 Mbit/s;
with the pods' 10 BSSs, beacons alone held channel 6 47 % busy.

The Banana Pi R4 runs mac80211 (mt76), as the lab does
(mac80211_hwsim): the platform now sets PLATFORM_FLAGS_SET_BSS and
sends the BSS parameters as hostapd does. That path's MLO link ID is
0047's, which this patch needs.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 platform/banana-pi/platform.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/platform/banana-pi/platform.c
+++ b/platform/banana-pi/platform.c
@@ -724,7 +724,12 @@ int platform_flags_init(int *flags)
 int platform_flags_init(int *flags)
 {
     wifi_hal_dbg_print("%s:%d \n",__func__,__LINE__);
-    *flags = PLATFORM_FLAGS_STA_INACTIVITY_TIMER | PLATFORM_FLAGS_CONTROL_PORT_FRAME;
+    /* mac80211 (mt76, mac80211_hwsim): the BSS's basic rates, ERP and HT protection go to the
+     * kernel with NL80211_CMD_SET_BSS, as hostapd sends them; without them mac80211 sends
+     * beacons, broadcasts and probe responses at the band's lowest rate (1 Mbit/s on 2.4 GHz)
+     * while the beacons advertise OFDM-only basic rates. */
+    *flags = PLATFORM_FLAGS_SET_BSS | PLATFORM_FLAGS_STA_INACTIVITY_TIMER |
+             PLATFORM_FLAGS_CONTROL_PORT_FRAME;
     return 0;
 }
 
